  "summary": "Claire Lomas, a 44-year-old charity campaigner who became paralyzed from the chest down after a riding accident in 2007, has died following an accident in Jordan. Known for her resilience, she raised nearly £1m for charity and completed marathons in a bionic suit, including the 2012 London Marathon in 17 days. She also lit the Paralympic cauldron in 2012 and participated in the Great North Run while pregnant in 2016. Her family has requested privacy as they grieve."
